STEP 2 -- E8 chain a0_MEASURED -> H0  (BOTH footings)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Footing A (canonical):    H0 = Z a0 / (c sqrt(Omega_L)),  Omega_L=0.6847 (Planck)
  Footing B (Pythagorean):  H0 = sqrt((Z a0/c)^2 + omega_m*(100)^2), omega_m=0.1430

  [ALL distances | Footing A canonical]
    a0_MEASURED = 1.588e-10 (+/- 20% boot) -> H0 = 114.3 km/s/Mpc (68% boot: 94.8 - 140.7)
    pair-scatter band maps to H0 in [58.6, 241.0] km/s/Mpc

  [ALL distances | Footing B Pythagorean]
    a0_MEASURED = 1.588e-10 (+/- 20% boot) -> H0 = 101.9 km/s/Mpc (68% boot: 87.1 - 122.4)
    pair-scatter band maps to H0 in [61.5, 203.0] km/s/Mpc

  [TRGB/Cepheid subset | Footing A canonical]
    a0_MEASURED = 1.155e-10 (+/- 20% boot) -> H0 = 83.2 km/s/Mpc (68% boot: 74.9 - 108.8)
    pair-scatter band maps to H0 in [58.3, 176.8] km/s/Mpc

  [TRGB/Cepheid subset | Footing B Pythagorean]
    a0_MEASURED = 1.155e-10 (+/- 20% boot) -> H0 = 78.5 km/s/Mpc (68% boot: 72.6 - 97.6)
    pair-scatter band maps to H0 in [61.3, 151.1] km/s/Mpc

  CIRCULARITY EXPOSURE (NOT a measurement):
    canonical a0=9.36e-11 is ITSELF Planck-anchored; feeding it to E8 gives
      Footing A -> H0 = 67.4   Footing B -> H0 = 67.4  (input recovery of 67.4)
    -> the ladder-free number is ONLY the a0_MEASURED -> H0 path above.

